==Strategy==
This stage is filled to the brim with a limited assortment of buffed Angels that cover The Perfect Cyclone's small blindspot, making the main threat extremely difficult to engage. Furthermore, Sleipnir's attacks can push units that already made it inside the blindspot into The Perfect Cyclone's effective range if it does not kill them outright. For this reason, using any units that outrange The Perfect Cyclone would be optimal, and the same goes for ones that could get reliable damage on the Angels. If using a conventional strategy, you'll likely wait until Sleipnir gets ahead of The Perfect Cyclone then slowly chip it with backliner-ranged units before finishing The Perfect Cyclone.

It's advised to avoid hitting the base until you have the Hippoes and Gory dealt with.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: Fully upgrading Cyberpunk Cat's Slow Talent makes it exceptionally useful, as its 1200 standing range keeps itself safe while delaying the already slow main threats from advancing, although its massive 800 range blindspot must be accounted for. Stacking a few more Cyberpunks could potentially eliminate any slow downtime, buying you all the time you need to clear the Angels.
*[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]]: Stacking this with Cyberpunk can create the ultimate wall against this stage, as this combined with a max slow talent Cyberpunk gives it almost 100% uptime. Combine it with another Cyberpunk and the stage is basically over, though this may not be optimal for strategies that involve luring the Sleipnir into the blindspot, as Deadeye will KB the Sleipnir.
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: Ramen is useful for stalling the Angels in any situation, although its slow speed makes it less than desirable when fighting The Perfect Cyclone as the Cyclone can cut down a lot of its HP quickly and destroy it, though thanks to his naturally high bulk he can sustain more hits than Dual Erasers against Perfect Cyclone and Angelic Sleipnir.
*[[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]]/[[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic King Dragon]]/[[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]]/[[Brainwashed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Dragon Cat]]: Used in many Uberless strategies, Dragon stacks rely on luring Sleipnir within their range and using something else to pin The Perfect Cyclone (standing range is identical to maximum effective range), slowly damaging Sleipnir and replacing the Dragons if they are destroyed. You'll have to be mindful of your resources when you use this, however, as Dragon variants are all expensive.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]]: An excellent complement to any strategy, Maglev's damage burst is best used with other attackers by letting them whittle Gabriel before sending it for the kill. Maglev's high speed ensures they can easily make it inside the blindspot, and if Sleipnir does not kill it quickly, it may get at least one extra hit for value.
*[[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]]: This defensive unit's main highlight is its very high health, singular knockback and its knockback immunity which prevents Sleipnir from pushing it. Its long cooldown means it should never be your only option, but when aided by others can create a thick line of defense.
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]]: Octopus' lower cooldown, singular knockback and resistance to Floating enemies makes it a great option for covering your other units against The Perfect Cyclone and helps to finish the stage with its ability to weaken Floating enemies.
*[[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]]: Allows you to almost infinitely stall a Heavenly Hippoe with the help of weaken combos. Perfect for stacking Long Distance units like Cyberpunk.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]]: Lufalan Pasalan has very long range (720), enough to reach The Perfect Cyclone safely. It also makes Sleipnir easier to deal with. And since you are fighting an endurance battle here, the Gabriels that come once in a while won't be that big of a problem despite its single target. Make sure it's spawned after the Angel waves die down and you should win from there with a bit of support.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Jizo's Mega Castle]]: While Kasa Jizo's first form may work well here, as most of the Angels have low range and its massive damage ability alongside its speed and disposability means they can be easily dealt with, the more recommended approach is to use his Evolved/True form as his better range allows him to outrange the Sleipnir and nuke it easily.
*[[Ushiwakamaru (Legend Rare Cat)|Colossal Benkei]]: Similar case to Kasa Jizo except he kills the Sleipnir EVEN faster.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Super Galaxy Cosmo]]: Super Galaxy Cosmo has extreme range (850), and its knockback ability can assist in regaining ground as all threats in the stage are within its target traits. It's best used as a supportive unit however due to the very slow attack rate. In True Form, Ultima Galaxy Cosmo's ability to additionally freeze them can buy a large window of opportunity for your units to attack and make a huge difference.
*[[Squirtgun Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Aquabuster Saki]]: Another great backliner for this stage, Aquabuster Saki targets only Floating and Angel threats at extreme range with equally extreme impact (500-900 effective Range, stands at 600). She can't outrange The Perfect Cyclone, but can still avoid Sleipnir and snipe them alongside everything else.
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]]: Dealing massive damage to everything traited through LD attacks that reach up to 1000 range, Phonoa can eat through everything while comfortably sitting behind, using the durable frontline Angels as setup, which enables it to hit The Perfect Cyclone from behind cover without coming under fire.
*[[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]]: Similar to Phonoa, but instead of massive damage to everything, does support damage and can slow everything for 2 seconds with mini-surges making it last longer. Also can use his lower damage to use the Gabriels as a reliable stepping stone.
*[[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]]: With Divine Kai μ's massive health pool she is able to get into the blindspot of the cyclone fairly easy, but you have to beware of Sleipnir's high damage, which might kill her before she is able to kill the Cyclone. Luckily, Kai has a decently short cooldown, allowing you to deploy another if the first is killed.
*[[Tekachi (Uber Rare Cat)|Adamankachi]]: Effectively a solid wall with their high health and [[Dodge]] against Floating and Angel. Although their chance to Dodge is somewhat low, the rapid attacks from the cyclone and Sleipnir will cause it to occur often; preventing the latter's knockback. Their attack power is fairly low, however, so other units should be used to defeat the duo.

